# Embed-asset upgrade blocklist — one <base> per line to HOLD a renet-embedded
# binary at its current Dockerfile pin instead of tracking upstream latest.
#
# Base names match the Dockerfile ARG <BASE>_VERSION, lowercased:
#   criu rsync rclone zot k3s csiprovisioner csisnapshotter snapshotcontroller
#
# Each entry needs a substantive BLOCKER reason (>=30 chars, no banned phrases),
# exactly like every other suppression list in this repo. Format:
#
#   # BLOCKER: <why this component is pinned back and when to revisit>
#   <base>
#
# Empty by default — nothing is held; every pin tracks upstream.

# BLOCKER: k3s 1.37.0+k3s1 is a MINOR bump to a binary renet EMBEDS, and three
# CI lanes execute it -- E2E K8s, E2E K8s Ceph and E2E K8s Multinode. Taking it
# means rebuilding the renet builder image, moving the SHA256 pin and
# AssetK3sVersion in private/renet/pkg/embed/embed.go, and re-deriving
# credits.go plus third-party-credits.json: a submodule change whose blast
# radius is the cluster lanes themselves. Branch 0914-1 / PR #589 is a CI-repair
# wave that took Quality / Security from 56 failures to an intermittent-flake
# hunt, and an embedded runtime upgrade landing beside it would make any red in
# those lanes ambiguous between the upgrade and the repair -- the one thing this
# wave has spent its whole length disentangling.
# REVISIT WHEN PR #589 MERGES: delete this line, run
# `npm run check:ci-embed-asset-freshness -- --upgrade`, then follow the four
# steps that gate prints. The pin is 1.36.4+k3s1 as of 2026-09-16.
k3s
